# Shell scripts and systemd units are consumed by Linux, which treats a
# trailing carriage return as part of the token. A CRLF shebang fails as
# "/usr/bin/env: bash\r: No such file or directory", and a CRLF unit file gives
# equally unhelpful parse errors. Contributors on Windows have core.autocrlf
# enabled by default, so pin these rather than relying on everyone's local
# configuration being kind.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.path text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf
